# v8.13.3 — AN ALLOW-LIST: exclude EVERYTHING, then re-admit exactly what the
# image runs.
#
# This file used to be a deny-list, and a deny-list fails OPEN on whatever nobody
# thought to list. Measured with a `FROM scratch; COPY . /ctx` export of the
# build context, it shipped:
#   - ./backups/<timestamp>/ — scripts/backup.sh's DEFAULT output, inside the
#     checkout the documented deploy builds from: the live database, both HMAC
#     secrets (.grading-secret, .unsubscribe-secret), logs and attachments;
#   - smoke-data-*/, data-harness-*/, uploads-test-worker-*/, .coverage/ — local
#     test artefacts, two of them holding a database and a .superadmin-password;
#   - a backup tarball written into the checkout, and AUTH_PATHS.md, EMAIL_RULES.md,
#     ROLES_AND_PERMISSIONS.md and ci/, all added after the list was written.
# A line per artefact is a list that is always one release behind. An allow-list
# fails CLOSED: anything new at the repo root stays out until somebody decides it
# belongs in the image.
#
# What the runtime reads, from code: server.js and db.js; lib/ and routes/ (every
# relative require resolves under them); version.json (lib/config requires it);
# public/ and docs/ (served, read through path.join(__dirname, …)). package.json
# and package-lock.json are what the build stage installs from, and the CI image
# (ci/Dockerfile.cross-browser, built from this same context) copies those two
# and nothing else. The Dockerfile and this file are read by the builder through
# its own channel, so excluding them changes nothing.
#
# A Docs-hygiene lock DERIVES that set from the code and both Dockerfiles and
# requires this list to equal it in both directions: a missing root is an image
# that cannot boot, an extra one is a decision nobody took. Stated limit: a file
# dropped INSIDE public/ or docs/ still ships — both are tracked trees.
#
# v8.13.4 — ONE BUILD-STAGE TOOL, ADMITTED AS A FILE, NOT AS A ROOT.
# scripts/prune-runtime-deps.cjs strips the native addons' build residue in the
# Dockerfile's build stage (tests/prune-runtime-deps.spec.js). It is re-admitted
# by its own path because scripts/ also holds backup.sh, purge.sh, smoke.cjs and
# the rest, none of which belongs in an image; and since `COPY . /src` mirrors
# the context, the build stage deletes /src/scripts before the runtime stage
# copies /src, so the image never carries it. The lock accepts a sub-path here
# only when it is exactly a file the app Dockerfile COPYs.
*
!server.js
!db.js
!version.json
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!lib/
!routes/
!public/
!docs/
!scripts/prune-runtime-deps.cjs
